From 14adbaf28012e4c3f241b20f0eef0bfe99817e98 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:29:50 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): Sodick Mark 21 header names its control and its
 threading

The Sodick wire post header now names the Mark 21 / EX21 control. It
warns LN1W / LN2W owners that G21 alarms (E00170) and the taper words
differ, and it points them to the Sodick Wire EDM (LN2W) post. The post
description says the same.

The threading line now matches the program. With AWT it reads
"PROGRAM THREADS THE WIRE WITH T91 AT START". Without AWT it says the
operator threads the wire at the M00.

Only comment lines and the description change. Every code line of the
eight goldens is byte-identical.

Fixes #4046
Fixes #4044

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
